KZ3 patch 1062 (SPU pass 47, finding RE pass 104; DEFAULT ON since SPU pass 60 with patches 1074 + 1077, KZ3_SPURS_ATTR_SDK=0 = the old 2/2 mapping): the HLE _cellSpursAttributeInitialize (NID 0x95180230, the SDK's internal entry behind the cellSpursAttributeInitialize() macro) takes (attr, revision, sdkVersion, nSpus, spuPriority, ppuPriority, exitIfNoWork); the public five-argument prototype reads r4 (revision = 2) as nSpus, so KZ3's HiPrio (nSpus 5) and LoPrio (nSpus 1) instances both get 2 virtual SPUs. Mapping in libs/spurs/kz3_spurs_attr.h, OPT-IN KZ3_SPURS_ATTR_SDK=1: with the real counts this port's HiPrio kernel threads never see a ready workload and the boot hangs in the menu movie (runs spu-47n-a1/a2c), so the default stays the old mapping until the kernel-thread/lane model works with 5. Host test tools/spu/test_spurs_attr.sh. Upstream: on hold.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.15.0 (SPU pass 81): absorbed by PR310 in its default, kept for kz3_spurs_attr.h (used by 1064, 1074, test_spurs_attr) and the KZ3_SPURS_ATTR_SDK switch, drop later with them.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): context only (upstream v0.18.0 changed lines around the hunks; same change).

